# Run SpringProjectApplication. Start with a fresh process and execute in order.
# 0-2 min: input vs response model; map and monotonic ID.
# 2-5 min: GET + POST, validation before allocation, 201 and Location.
# 5-9 min: PUT and rejected update; GET proves the old movie is unchanged.
# 9-12 min: DELETE then POST proves IDs do not collide.
# 12-15 min: repeated POST vs PUT, missing IDs and empty list.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081

### Initially: 200 []
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies

### Invalid create: 400; does not consume ID 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":" ","releaseYear":2014}

### 201; ID 1; Location: /movies/1
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Inception","releaseYear":2010}

### 201; ID 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Interstellar","releaseYear":2014}

### 200: one movie
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### 200: replaces both details; ID remains 1. Repeat: same state.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"The Matrix","releaseYear":1999}

### 400: must NOT change title to Damaged
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Damaged","releaseYear":1800}

### Still The Matrix / 1999
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### 400: year required; not silently treated as zero
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Missing year"}

### 404: PUT cannot create a missing movie
PUT {{baseUrl}}/movies/999
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Missing","releaseYear":2020}

### 204: no response body
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### 201: ID 3, not 2. Repeat POST creates another movie with a new ID.
POST {{baseUrl}}/movies
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Arrival","releaseYear":2016}

### Movie 2 must still be Interstellar
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/2

### 404 after deletion
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### 404 on repeated delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/1

### Remove remaining movies to demonstrate 200 []
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/2

### 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/movies/3

### 200 []; if you repeated POST, also delete its returned ID first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/movies
